Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) has graduated from simple toy prototypes to foundational enterprise architecture. However, engineers quickly discover that naive vector similarity search fails in production. It suffers from the "vocabulary mismatch problem": a dense embedding model might miss exact SKU numbers, error codes, or legal terminologies that keyword-based algorithms catch instantly.

In this deep-dive guide, we will architect and implement an enterprise-grade **Generative AI RAG Pipeline** using **Node.js, TypeScript, Supabase `pgvector`**, and **Google's Gemini AI**. We will implement a robust hybrid search mechanism combining PostgreSQL's native `tsvector` (BM25-style keyword matching) with high-dimensional vector embeddings, re-ranked via Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF).

