## Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)

### Q1: Why use Hybrid Search instead of pure Vector Embeddings?
Pure vector search is fantastic for semantic similarity, but it routinely fails when exact keywords (such as specific error codes, API endpoints, UUIDs, or part serial numbers) are queried. Hybrid search bridges this gap by combining traditional lexical lookup with dense vector spaces.

### Q2: How does Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) work?
RRF assigns a score based on the position (rank) of a document in multiple retrieval lists rather than raw mathematical distance or probabilistic scores. This bypasses the difficulty of normalizing disparate score distributions between BM25 full-text rank and cosine similarity vector distance.

### Q3: Why choose Supabase `pgvector` for node-based apps?
By keeping vector workloads inside PostgreSQL, you avoid introducing separate dedicated vector databases (like Pinecone or Milvus). You retain ACID compliance, relational metadata filtering, and robust security policies (Row Level Security) under a single roof.

